A small child's arm wrapped in a bright white plaster cast, rendered in Vincent van Gogh's distinctive Post-Impressionist style with bold, swirling brushstrokes in vibrant yellows, blues, and greens. The cast is decorated with colorful marker doodles and small stickers. The background features a cozy living room scene with a low sofa bed, painted with thick impasto texture and dynamic, expressive movement in every surface. Warm afternoon light streams through a window, creating pools of golden ochre and deep violet shadows that dance across the scene. The mood is bittersweet yet tender, capturing childhood resilience and the small adventures of growing up. The perspective focuses intimately on the cast as a badge of honor, with soft toys and scattered crayons visible in the swirling background.
